**File whose own suggestions exceed the slot is never cut to fit**

A batch above `budget` is rejected for context overflow, so every suggestion for that file fails. Chunk `forFile` into slices that leave room for the patch instead of sending one oversized request.



<details>
<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>

````text
File libs/code-review/infrastructure/adapters/services/llmAnalysis.service.ts, lines 392-402:

File whose own suggestions exceed the slot is never cut to fit

When one file's own suggestions already exceed the slot budget, `own = budget - fixedFor(forFile)` is ≤ 0, so the `while (own > 0 && …)` cut is skipped entirely and the full section is pushed into its own batch. That batch is emitted far above `budget`, so the provider rejects it for context overflow and the whole file's suggestions fail (logged by the per-batch catch at line 249) — exactly the failure this PR set out to eliminate, and it stays reachable with a small BYOK window plus a few large `existingCode`/`improvedCode` suggestions on one hot file (the flush check at line 403 puts the oversized section alone in a batch, so it is not absorbed by another). Chunk the file's suggestion list so each slice leaves room for the patch instead of sending a request that is guaranteed to be rejected.

Suggested code:

// A file's own suggestions can alone exceed the slot: pack them
// into slices that each fit (leaving room for the patch section)
// instead of emitting a request the provider will reject.
const slices: Partial<CodeSuggestion>[][] = [];
let slice: Partial<CodeSuggestion>[] = [];
for (const s of forFile) {
    if (slice.length && fixedFor([...slice, s]) > budget * 0.9) {
        slices.push(slice);
        slice = [];
    }
    slice.push(s);
}
slices.push(slice);

for (const fileSlice of slices) {
    // … existing cut + flush body, measured against `fileSlice`
    // instead of `forFile` (a slice has own > 0 again) …
}
````

</details>


