**Group splitting re-tokenizes the growing group on every suggestion**

Re-measuring the whole growing group with `fixedFor([...group, suggestion])` costs O(k²) tokenizer work in k = suggestions, burning hundreds of milliseconds at ~40 suggestions and seconds of CPU at ~200 before any request is issued. Measure each suggestion once with `estimateTokens(JSON.stringify(suggestion))` and accumulate the group's fixed cost incrementally instead of re-tokenizing at every step.



<details>
<summary>Prompt for LLM</summary>

````text
File libs/code-review/infrastructure/adapters/services/llmAnalysis.service.ts, lines 419-428:

Group splitting re-tokenizes the growing group on every suggestion

The group-splitting loop re-measures the whole growing group on every suggestion with `fixedFor([...group, suggestion])`, so building the groups for one file costs O(k^2) tokenizer work in k = suggestions on that file (each concatenation is a new string, so the estimator's memo never hits). On a file carrying many sizeable suggestions — exactly the over-budget payload this PR exists for — this burns hundreds of milliseconds at ~40 suggestions and seconds of CPU at ~200 (tiktoken runs at roughly 15ms per 92k chars per the tokenizer's own note) before any request is issued. Measure each suggestion once and accumulate the group's fixed cost incrementally (per-suggestion `estimateTokens(JSON.stringify(suggestion))` plus the constant prompt overhead) instead of re-tokenizing `[...group, suggestion]` at every step.

Suggested code:

const fixedOverhead = fixedFor([]);
let groupTokens = 0;
for (const suggestion of forFile) {
    // Measure each suggestion once and accumulate the group's cost:
    // re-tokenizing the whole growing group per step is quadratic.
    const suggestionTokens = estimateTokens(
        JSON.stringify(suggestion),
    );
    if (
        group.length &&
        fixedOverhead + groupTokens + suggestionTokens > budget / 2
    ) {
        groups.push(group);
        group = [];
        groupTokens = 0;
    }
    group.push(suggestion);
    groupTokens += suggestionTokens;
}
````

</details>


